ircle with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2?$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300220 1113 #uuid "6ef5e6f3-6c45-5d98-acf4-10fcf48b2036" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300220 1145 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =2 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300222 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300223 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300224 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300225 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300226 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1041 "selection" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300223 13194139534638 true] [17592186300221 1110 #uuid "f02eb77d-ff25-5359-af01-58e5c835c0e8" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300222 1034 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $4$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534638 true] [17592186300222 1111 #uuid "ecd621df-259c-5ab7-b4f2-37364568cbb8" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300223 1034 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534638 true] [17592186300223 1111 #uuid "46e4a611-a047-562d-b22b-561da3e16df8" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300224 1034 "The center is $(2,2)$ and the radius is $2$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534638 true] [17592186300224 1111 #uuid "df159787-1b6d-5aad-b1f3-6f57e4e21fde" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300225 1034 "The center is $(2,2)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534638 true] [17592186300225 1111 #uuid "a250b950-8fa6-52d9-878d-8a2b2312a788" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300226 1034 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $2$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534638 true] [17592186300226 1111 #uuid "2784d62a-f4bf-562a-9e59-35592c9bfb8e" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300228 13194139534638 true] [17592186300227 1089 "q-116927" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534638 true] [17592186300227 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/343897550f0f7b9e4a479e47c9191ababa31070dac79dbf4d54befe869661a48.png)\n\nGiven that the points $X$ and $Y$ with coordinates $(-1,2)$ and $(1,-2),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300227 1113 #uuid "6871bb55-7096-5bdc-95c3-97647e61a9a8" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300227 1145 "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{XY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-1)^{2}+(2-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300229 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300230 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300231 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300232 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300233 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1041 "selection" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300230 13194139534638 true] [17592186300228 1110 #uuid "2486e628-9311-5fb6-8e2b-19781c671d57" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300229 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{10}" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300229 1111 #uuid "e35d3d6a-3b91-51ad-9f88-38c2843cdc6a" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300230 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300230 1111 #uuid "db0fd51e-e76c-555f-9699-f32217b057e6" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300231 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300231 1111 #uuid "528eb12a-a74e-5b28-a070-e12a4489bd19" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300232 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300232 1111 #uuid "333f8e35-2f38-5923-9acf-51563f336b96" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300233 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300233 1111 #uuid "a9382ecc-1a07-53cc-a109-22b49f37bfc7" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300234 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300235 13194139534638 true] [17592186300234 1089 "q-14559" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534638 true] [17592186300234 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/14af607cba7a2c47e8443857f5f3ed6ff33cd5fa2fb12e5d451eea08a932139a.png)\n\nGiven that the points $X$ and $Y$ with coordinates $(3,4)$ and $(-3,-4),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300234 1113 #uuid "08a7411b-9289-5682-bc33-79fdf3eacff1" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300234 1145 "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{XY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(3-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{10}{2}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300236 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300237 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300238 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300239 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300240 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1041 "selection" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300239 13194139534638 true] [17592186300235 1110 #uuid "021ccf57-4059-55f5-b193-fcbb451d844e" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300236 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=100" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300236 1111 #uuid "6778cf3d-0306-556d-9879-566cfa0f6f20" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300237 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534638 true] [17592186300237 1111 #uuid "b7c1258b-cb57-5a5d-97f3-d3a123597d7e" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300238 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" 13194139534638 true] [17592186300238 1103 #edb/ref 1759218